      },
      "message": "feat(kernel): a machining mesh from solidcore-tess with a measured deviation\n\nA solidcore-imported STEP solid is meshed by solidcore-tess at a chord in\nmm and handed out only whole and measured inside the tolerance:\n- every PlanStats shortfall that touches the guarantee (unmeshed, lenient,\n  unsampled edge, a face or edge capped off its tolerance) and every\n  evaluator refusal is a named MeshRefusal; the rest are report notes;\n- the deviation is sampled at 15 barycentric points a triangle, against\n  the plan surface at the same (u, v) and against the record face's\n  analytic surface in closed form; judged by the analytic distance where\n  the face is analytic, else the parametric one;\n- welded by exact position: no open, over-shared or turned side; positive\n  volume; the app's 30 M triangle budget; a tolerance under a millionth\n  of the body is refused, never quietly coarsened; a CancelToken bound.\n\nStepSolid keeps its reader record. solidcore-tess moves from a dev- to a\nlibrary dependency of the kernel (no new package); wasm32 checks clean.\nBench (kernel release lane): every fixture within 0.005 and 0.01 mm;\ntruck stands 9.99e-3 mm off on the metre file at the 0.005 cap.\nDecisions in docs/decisions/940-machining-mesh.md; follow-up #1029.\n\nFixes #940\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
